        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this superb three-bedroom, two-bathroom mid-terrace family home to the Finglas property market, ideally positioned within the ever-popular Charlestown Green development. No. 2 offers spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout, extending to approximately c. 102 sq.m, together with the added benefit of a converted attic, west-facing rear garden and an excellent location close to a fantastic range of local amenities.\n\nInternal accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hallway leading into a fully fitted kitchen, a downstairs toilet and a large living room to the rear. The living room provides direct access to the private west-facing rear garden, offering an excellent outdoor space for entertaining and relaxing. Upstairs there are two generous double bedrooms, with the main bedroom benefiting from built-in wardrobes, a single bedroom and a family bathroom. The property also benefits from a converted attic above, providing valuable additional space and excellent versatility for a variety of uses, subject to the necessary requirements. The property has been well maintained and provides a practical layout ideal for modern family living. Additional benefits include gas-fired central heating with a combi boiler, double glazed windows throughout.\n\nCharlestown Green is ideally positioned within easy reach of the excellent amenities available at Charlestown Shopping Centre, including a wide selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, a cinema, pharmacy, gym and various other services and facilities. Finglas Village is also within easy reach, providing further shopping, dining, educational and recreational amenities. There is an excellent selection of local schools, parks, sporting clubs and leisure facilities in the surrounding area, while DCU, IKEA, Clearwater Shopping Centre and The National Botanic Gardens are all easily accessible.\n\nThe location is exceptionally well serviced by public transport, with numerous Dublin Bus routes and local bus stops within easy walking distance, providing frequent access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The M50, M1, N2 and N3 are all easily accessible, while Dublin Airport is also within a convenient commuting distance, making this an ideal location for first-time buyers, families and commuters alike.\n\nContact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0861985247 or 015411455 to arrange a viewing or for further information.\n\nAdditional Features:\n• BER C1\n• c. 102 sq.m\n• Three-bedroom, two-bathroom mid-terrace family home\n• Converted attic providing valuable additional space\n• Downstairs toilet\n• Family bathroom\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Combi boiler\n• Double glazed windows throughout\n• Entrance hallway\n• Fully fitted kitchen\n• Large living room\n• Direct access to west-facing rear garden\n• Two generous double bedrooms\n• Main bedroom with built-in wardrobes\n• Spacious single bedroom\n• Private west-facing rear garden\n• Excellent family accommodation\n• Bright and well-proportioned throughout\n• Excellent potential and versatility\n• Mature and highly sought-after residential location\n• Short distance to Charlestown Shopping Centre\n• Excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and supermarkets\n• Cinema, gym, pharmacy and numerous local services nearby\n• Close to Finglas Village\n• Excellent selection of local schools and amenities\n• Numerous bus stops within walking distance\n• Well serviced by Dublin Bus routes\n• Easy access to Dublin City Centre\n• Convenient access to M50, M1, N2 and N3\n• Dublin Airport within easy reach\n• Close to IKEA, Clearwater Shopping Centre, DCU and National Botanic Gardens"
      },
